  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The sulphide ore of iron is iron pyrite.</p><p>Iron can be extracted from iron pyrites</p><p><b>Galena</b>&nbsp;is the sulphide ore&nbsp;of lead (PbS)</p><p>The sulphide containing ore of zinc is zinc blende <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ZnS</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math> is extracted from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> i.e., Bauxite ore</p><p>Hence, Iron, lead and zinc can be extracted from their sulphide ores but not aluminium.</p></blockquote>",
